    "md5": "e5cc95265cc56a286279ad6e98cb3df9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1411,
    "chunk_text": "The conflict did not start with Tamil youth taking up arms. The conflict started way before that, just after Independence, when majority vote was used, when majoritarian tendencies showed to even deprive a part of\n\n899 900\n\n2024 \u0db8\u0dd0\u0dd2 07\n\nthe citizenry of this country their basic citizenship right. Six members of the up-country Tamil community who were Members of the House lost their citizenship rights! That is when majoritarian rule gave its notice to the others; that is why the political party that I belong to was born. That is why we said, \"Share governance powers so that even those who are not a majority in the whole of the country but a majority, at least, in the areas they live in could look after their day-to-day affairs\". There are affairs that only the Central Government can look after. No, we do not want that. Let the Central Government, in which we also participate, look after those matters.\n\nBut, with regard to matters that are down to earth, matters that could happen, the principle of subsidiarity must prevail. What could be done in Monaragala need not be decided in Colombo; it must be decided there. So, that is the basic idea of devolution of power, that people, in their own localities, must make decisions with regard to their areas. That should be done properly. That is the basic cry of the Tamil-speaking people of this country, that you share power in a meaningful way."
