    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "7249a6b62fc34c51b548ef20f225518b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2095,
    "chunk_text": "Whereupon THE HON. SAMANPRIYA HERATH left the Chair and THE HON. KINS NELSON took the Chair.\n\n[2.37 p.m.] \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dd3\u0db8\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0db1 \u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0dda \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc7\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc7\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc6\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0bb1\u0bb5\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) Bismillahir Rahmanir Raheem.\n\nThis extraordinary avenue that is available to banks in case of defaulting loans, which was only restricted to the State banks way back in the 1990s, was extended to the private, commercial banks as well. The Government has now agreed to look into that parate execution law and has brought this particular Amendment to suspend the operation of that law until the end of this year. But, we are proposing an Amendment to extend it by a further year so that the relief could have a meaningful impact on our local businesses. However, when doing this, we have also got to be careful that we do not assist the serial defaulters.\n\nI also must take exception to the fact that some in the banking sector have been talking about other stakeholders being impacted on. That is, particularly the depositors in the banks. I do not fully agree with that contention. I would say that it is because the banks want to safeguard their shareholders. The banks have been given enough assistance. Finally, the entire EPF had to bear the brunt of the domestic debt restructuring fiasco, which once again went to assist the commercial banks in the country. They have been able to retain their profits and beyond that, there is a massive amount allocated to bailout the banks in financial stress as well. So, with all these benefits, it is incumbent on the banks to treat these small and medium industries, which are in serious distress, through this particular relief measure that the Government has proposed. Therefore, I welcome that move. In the meantime, it would be useful for the Government also to assess those serial defaulters prior to 2019, have a database and not allow them to benefit from this particular space that is being given to everybody as carte blanche."
  },
