    "md5": "0f207ee80dc750afde301f76320b7cf9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1677,
    "chunk_text": "Given the above, Sri Lanka has signed Host Country Agreements with the ICRAF on 14th September, 2022 and with the GGGI, on 07th February, 2023. Sri Lanka also intends to accede to the Agreement on the Privileges and Immunities of the IAEA. That is, the International Atomic Energy Agency. In order to give effect to the provisions relating to privileges and immunities in the Agreements signed with ICRAF and the GGGI and the IAEA Agreement to be acceded to, I, Minister of Foreign Affairs, by Orders in Gazette Extraordinary No. 2348/48 dated 08th September, 2023 published the said provisions in keeping with Section 4 of the Diplomatic Privileges Act, No. 09 of 1996. Also, in keeping with Section 5 of the Diplomatic Privileges Act, No. 09 of 1996, the provisions relating to the privileges and immunities published by the Orders are now placed before Parliament for approval.\n\n(i) Sustainable management of the upper watershed for better management of erosion and water resources.\n\nApproximately, a US Dollars 40 million GCF grant project was developed with the support of ICRAF together with the International Union for Conservation of Nature - IUCN. The executive entities for the GCF Knuckles Project are, ICRAF\n\nand the Ministry of Irrigation and the project is implemented in partnership with several other key Ministries, including the Ministry of Environment as the National Designated Authority for GCF.\n\nii. Development of four transformational projects under the Readiness Grant including an estimated US Dollars 150 million project that aims to develop export value chains based on improved varieties of under-invested tree crops such as jack, kithul et cetera."
  },
