    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "8bb1aeb98107565de84df1d99907c3d8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1559,
    "chunk_text": "ii. Development of four transformational projects under the Readiness Grant including an estimated US Dollars 150 million project that aims to develop export value chains based on improved varieties of under-invested tree crops such as jack, kithul et cetera.\n\nThe GGGI is a treaty-based international, intergovernmental organization that is dedicated to supporting and promoting strong, inclusive and sustainable economic growth in developing countries and emerging economies. Its mission is to support members in the transformation of their economies into a green growth economic model. The GGGI plays the role of an enabler and facilitator for the transition of its member countries into low-carbon green economies by providing policy and technical support in the development of green growth plans, support in mobilization of green investments, implementation of green growth projects with identified key national entities and development of local capacities and knowledge sharing.\n\nThe GGGI has a Framework Agreement with the Green Climate Fund - GCF - for their Readiness Programme. The GCF, the Green Climate Fund, is the largest fund in the world in relation to climate change. At present, the GGGI is the delivery partner for the GCF National Adaptation Planning Readiness Support Project and is working closely with the Ministry of Environment on revising Sri Lanka's National Adaptation Plan - NAP - for 2025-2034 and preparing Sri Lanka\u2019s first set of Provincial Adaptation Plans - PAPs - and investment plans for all nine provinces in Sri Lanka."
  },
