    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "b1a8d1c813c0d01aab9c973605740683",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2067,
    "chunk_text": "The GGGI has a Framework Agreement with the Green Climate Fund - GCF - for their Readiness Programme. The GCF, the Green Climate Fund, is the largest fund in the world in relation to climate change. At present, the GGGI is the delivery partner for the GCF National Adaptation Planning Readiness Support Project and is working closely with the Ministry of Environment on revising Sri Lanka's National Adaptation Plan - NAP - for 2025-2034 and preparing Sri Lanka\u2019s first set of Provincial Adaptation Plans - PAPs - and investment plans for all nine provinces in Sri Lanka.\n\nIn addition to being the delivery partner on the revision of the National Adaptation Plan, the ongoing initiatives in Sri Lanka by the GGGI will include\n\n1041 1042\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0d91\u0db8\u0dca.\u0dba\u0dd6.\u0d91\u0db8\u0dca. \u0d85\u0dd2\u0db8 \u0dcf.\u0dbb\u0dd2 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2024 \u0db8\u0dd0\u0dba\u0dd2 08\n\nfacilitating the adoption of sustainable public transport services - e-mobility - for low-carbon city development in the Colombo Metropolitan area and exploration of renewable energy investment opportunities. So, those are two very important institutions which are setting up their Country Offices in Sri Lanka. In terms of our obligation, we are providing them with certain privileges and immunities so that they would be comfortable here in dealing with the Government and the agencies of the Government.\n\nWhy are we giving these privileges and immunities to the IAEA? The IAEA is the world\u2019s intergovernmental forum for scientific and technical co-operation to secure peaceful and safe use of nuclear science and technology and nuclear power, which contributes to the UN Sustainable Development Goals.\n\nThe IAEA was established as an autonomous international organization under the UN system on 29th July, 1957 and Sri Lanka has been a founding member since 1957. Though established independently of the United Nations, through its own international Treaty, the IAEA reports to both the United Nations General Assembly and the Security Council and is headquartered in Vienna, Austria."
  },
