    "md5": "3e0ffa89db53a4b3cee5eede775b50db",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2059,
    "chunk_text": "The vehicles in the institute\u2019s pool are used for field inspections and a list of them has been given in Annex 09*. As these vehicles are used for the functions of the entire institution, in cases where field inspections are not sufficient, vehicles are obtained on rent via the online system upon the approval of the institution.\n\n1355 1356\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dca \u200d\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2024 \u0db8\u0dd0\u0dba\u0dd2 09\n\nMaking payments for field inspections\n\nNo separate fee is charged for field inspections and in submitting online applications, an amount of Rs. 2,662.74 with taxes is charged as per each category for all administrative activities i.e. issuance of certificates/permits or an amount of Rs. 1,331.28 is charged for issuing temporary certificates.\n\nAn amount of Rs.12,102.00 is charged as administrative fees for the issuance of licences to the institutions recommended based on the results of the field inspection and the amount published on the website according to the respective category and number of rooms. It ranges from Rs. 2,420.51 to Rs. 70,194.87.\n\nOfficers conducting field inspections are paid an allowance of Rs. 5,000 per day and an allowance of Rs. 3,000 for food and around 10 institutions are inspected daily. The number of institutions that can be checked will be determined according to the respective categories and the distance of the locations. During a field inspection for a few days, the same officials will make payments for the accommodation facilities and then after checking the bills, the money will be reimbursed.\n\n(v) Temporary certificates are not issued or\n\ncertificates issued are not extended without inspection. During the periods when it was not possible to do field inspections, extensions were made based on the photographic data so that the service providers would not be harmed and by now, all those places have been subjected to field inspections and shortcomings have been pointed out or places have been recommended. The places where the shortcomings are rectified are re- inspected."
