    "chunk_size_bytes": 1830,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dba\u0db1\u0db1\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bc7\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc7\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc1\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bc6\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Chairman of Committees) Next, the Hon. M.A. Sumanthiran. [1.45 pm.] \u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0d91\u0db4.\u0d92. \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc7\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc7\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd.\u0b8f. \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0bc7\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba9\u0bcd) (The Hon. M.A. Sumanthiran) Thank you, Hon. Deputy Chairman of Committees, for the opportunity given to say a few words.\n\nI must also mention one other matter. When he was the Chief Minister of the first Provincial Council of Wayamba, he showed the rest of the country what provincial councils, even with their limited powers, could do. He enacted so many legislations including the Statute on environment, which is a classic example of how even a provincial legislation could override the Central Government legislation on that area. To date, it is the legislation that is in force. So, he showed us the way.\n\nWe asked for devolution of power and provincial councils were established consequent to the Indo-Lanka Accord. Unfortunately, at that time, the North-East Provincial Council had been dissolved, but in the rest of\n\n1431 1432\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d89\u0db8\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dba\u0ddc \u0dca \u0db6\u0ddc\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0dbb\u0dca \u0db8\u0ddc\u0d9a\u0ddc\u0dbb\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc]\n\n2024 \u0db8\u0dbd\u0dba\u0dd2 10\n\nthe country, the provincial councils functioned and Wayamba was the flagship. It led the way and showed what could be done even with all the shortcomings in the Thirteenth Amendment.\n\nSo, for those two reasons, I wish to, on behalf of the people of the North and the East, record my condolences on the demise of the Hon. Gamini Jayawickrama Perera and request that these sentiments also be communicated to his family. Thank you."
  },
