    "md5": "e61e9c53309fce7f6cb28cb42114c4ae",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1680,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Speaker, for the foregoing reasons and since there is the second Nakba now taking place particularly in the Rafah Region of the Gaza Strip, this Parliament urges the international community, through all means available, be it the UN General Assembly, the Security Council, the International Court of Justice or the International Criminal Court, to forthwith ensure a permanent ceasefire, punish the perpetrators as war criminals and guarantee the setting up of an independent, sovereign Palestine.\n\nThe founding ideology of the ethnonational Jewish State contained a few Palestinians and they would have ideally wanted no Palestinians to exist within the Israeli Territory. But, the fact remains that there is the Gaza Strip now, there is the West Bank, there is East Jerusalem and that there is also quite a number - almost 30 per cent - of Arabs living within the State of Israel apart from the West Bank, the Gaza Strip and the Golan Heights.\n\nTherefore, Sir, it is now time for us to call this to a halt. In this regard, it is important for us to realize the whole attempt by Prime Minister Netanyahu with his original pledge that he will free the hostages. None of us want the hostages to be harmed and all the peace-loving people in the world want all those hostages to be released. We make that appeal to Hamas, to see that they are released unharmed. But, unfortunately, there may be a few, who would have already met with their deaths. Then, recently, the Egyptian negotiators, along with the Qatari negotiators, came to negotiate with Hamas and the Israeli demand to release all the hostages, both civilian and\n\n1675 1676\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0"
  },
  {
