    "md5": "05ae13eb79cfa1bfa2be3fe46538d342",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1240,
    "chunk_text": "Therefore, Sir, it is now time for us to call this to a halt. In this regard, it is important for us to realize the whole attempt by Prime Minister Netanyahu with his original pledge that he will free the hostages. None of us want the hostages to be harmed and all the peace-loving people in the world want all those hostages to be released. We make that appeal to Hamas, to see that they are released unharmed. But, unfortunately, there may be a few, who would have already met with their deaths. Then, recently, the Egyptian negotiators, along with the Qatari negotiators, came to negotiate with Hamas and the Israeli demand to release all the hostages, both civilian and\n\n1675 1676\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nBy yesterday, even the Egyptian Government has publicly announced that they will support the South African demand to haul up the Israeli Government. That is, for the case before the ICJ, the Egyptians will also start supporting. It is unfortunate that many countries in the region still maintain diplomatic relations with Israel despite the fact that such atrocities are taking place. Therefore, in the name of humanity, we are requesting that even we take a bold stand against what is happening today in Gaza."
