    "md5": "1fcfe616408c79461817628d8deb328d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1879,
    "chunk_text": "The situation that prevails in Palestine today is horrible, a very serious issue and cannot be ignored by any civilized country or people. Sir, while I speak on that issue, I will also refer, later in my speech, to the doublespeak and hypocrisy shown by the Members of this House as they debated this issue. Much was said about the hypocrisy of the West, the white supremacists and I concur with those sentiments. The world is aghast at the blatant hypocrisy that the western nations promote or pay lip service to human rights, the international humanitarian law, genocide, persecution and international crimes of that nature. They are turning a blind eye, not only just\n\nturning a blind eye but they are also supporting State terrorism that is being prosecuted by the State of Israel on the hapless people of Palestine.\n\nIt is also important to note that there is a complicit arrangement between Hamas and the State of Israel, much the same way the Easter Sunday bombings happened in this country. It is always useful for leaders of countries whose popularity is dipping to show an enemy of the State and then become popular on that. This is the most heinous way of remaining in power. We have seen that happening in our country, too. But, what is happening in Palestine is being exposed by the right-thinking people in the western nations today, not only those in the western nations, but also by the right-thinking Jewish people. I have seen a video of a Holocaust survivor who says, \u201cNot in my name, not in our name\u201d and he explains how what is happening today is very similar to what he and others had to undergo under the Nazi regime. He cites similarities and says, \u201cHow can I support this? This cannot be done in my name.\" Yes, the Holocaust was a horrible thing that happened to the Jews. But, what they are doing now to the people in Palestine is exactly similar."
