    "chunk_text": "What is happening today is so sad that a race which was almost annihilated - six million of them perished - and which gave rise to the concept of genocide themselves are now doing this to the others. This must stop. And, we, so far away from that theatre, are concerned and we must be concerned. That is not an internal affair of Israel, as much as what happened in this country is not an internal affair of Sri Lanka. When international crimes are committed, it is an international concern. We are hypocritical when we say what happened in Sri Lanka is an internal matter for Sri Lanka,\n\n1697 1698\n\n2024 \u0db8\u0dd0\u0dba\u0dd2 1\n\nbut what happens in Palestine is not an internal matter for Israel. That is also a doublespeak I want to expose, not only the doublespeak of the West.\n\nIt is a matter of regret that the Mover of this Adjournment Motion, the Hon. Rauff Hakeem, was the Minister of Justice who went to UN Human Rights Council and defended the State of Sri Lanka. And today, he is moving that Benjamin Netanyahu be tried before the ICC. Why not President Mahinda Rajapaksa, why not President Gotabaya Rajapaksa and why not all those who were in that chain of command who perpetrated that violence, those genocidal acts and the persecution on our people? You want Heads of State of other countries tried before the ICC. The ICC is good for you also when it is for the other person; international intervention is good for you. You call for a UN intervention for the others, but not"
