    "md5": "0b0afd1651583e733253e8ffba82b5d3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1501,
    "chunk_text": "While recognizing the legitimate and sensitive security concerns of both the Palestinian and Israeli people, we support the diplomatic efforts to find a lasting solution to the conflict and request both parties to engage in a dialogue to achieve durable peace. The two States living side by side in harmony with one another within secured borders is key to achieving long-term security, peace and prosperity. I wish to reiterate the importance of the early implementation of the United Nations General Assembly Resolutions regarding a two-State solution on the basis of the 1967 borders.\n\nLast year, my Minister met His Excellency Mahmoud Abbas, the President of the Palestinian National Authority and assured Sri Lanka\u2019s steadfast support for the Palestinian cause. Since 1968, Sri Lanka, as the Chair of the United Nations Special Committee to Investigate Israeli Practices Affecting the Human Rights of the\n\n1785 1786\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dad\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0db6\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dc3\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2024 \u0db8\u0dd0\u0dba\u0dd2 1\n\nPalestinian People and Other Arabs of the Occupied Territories, has been one of the most significant voices at the United Nations on the subject of the unfortunate conditions of the people in the Occupied Territories.\n\nSir, perpetration of violence and terrorism, in all its forms and manifestations, should be condemned. All acts of violence and terrorism are criminal and unjustifiable, regardless of their motivation and for whatever reason and wherever those are committed and by whoever."
  },
