    "md5": "0fc192db025788de85905304cdc5c644",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2289,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, perpetration of violence and terrorism, in all its forms and manifestations, should be condemned. All acts of violence and terrorism are criminal and unjustifiable, regardless of their motivation and for whatever reason and wherever those are committed and by whoever.\n\nSri Lanka remains committed to supporting a negotiated settlement in line with the relevant UN Resolutions leading to two States living side by side based on the 1967 borders.\n\nUntil everyone enjoys peace, no one will be safe. Therefore, disproportionate use of power and suppression of legitimate rights of any people or community would only escalate further tensions and create a situation where security of both Palestinians and Israelis are threatened with the possibility of violence escalating and spreading into other regions. Therefore, Sri Lanka once again urges all parties to act with restraint and to respect human rights\n\nand act in a manner which advances humanity. The international community also has a huge responsibility in implementing the UN Resolutions without hindrance and must act towards attaining long-lasting peace in the region on the basis of those Resolutions.\n\nI wish to place on record that the Sri Lankan Government continues to extend support to the Palestine Mission in Colombo. The Government of Sri Lanka, reflecting its solidarity with the Palestine people, also maintains a Representative Office in Ramallah.\n\nSir, we reaffirm our resolute support for the Palestinian cause as the people of Palestine strive to gain their legitimate rights and aspirations. Once again, let me endorse our solidarity with the Palestinian people in achieving their inalienable rights and establishing an independent, sovereign State based on the relevant UN Resolutions.\n\nThank you. \u0d91\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc4\u0dd2 \u0dc0\u0dda\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc0 \u0d85.\u0dc0\u0dcf. 5.30 \u0db1\u0dc0\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dca \u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dc1\u0dba\u0dd3\u0dba\u0db1\u0db1\u0dba \u0dc0\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db8 \u0dcf \u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dc0 \u0d9a\u0dca \u0dad\u0db6\u0db1 \u0dbd\u0daf\u0dd3.\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dc0 \u0d8a \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0d9a\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dc0, \u0d85\u0daf \u0dd2\u0dbb\u0db1 \u0dc0\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dca\u0db8\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dba \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dc0, 2024 \u0db8\u0dd0\u0dba\u0dd2 22\u0dc0\u0db1 \u0db6\u0daf\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dcf \u0db4\u0dd6.\u0dc0\u0dcf. 9.30 \u0dc0\u0db1 \u0dc0\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dca \u0d9c\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dda \u0dba."
