    "chunk_text": "Finance - my Colleague the Hon. (Dr.) Suren Raghavan is also here - proposed to this House that a voucher be provided to them. The original estimate was about Rs. 11 billion based on the calculations we had made. Subsequently, after many discussions in the Committee on Public Finance, in the Women Parliamentarians\u2019 Caucus and with the staff concerned of the Hon. Ministry of Education, the Ministry of Defence and the Ministry of Finance, the Hon. Minister of Education has allocated Rs. 1 billion starting from this week to provide vouchers for 800,000 school-going women.\n\nHon. Minister, my point is, do not start the programme by giving it to just 800,000 school girls. You say that you are going to focus on schools in difficult and rural areas. But, my suggestion is this, Hon. Minister. There are school-going, young women in Obeysekarapura and Bandaranayakapura in my area, Kotte, too, who cannot afford to buy such products. So, it does not have to be only school girls in rural areas; it does not have to be only\n\n195 196\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0dcf\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dba) \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dc2 \u0daf \u0dc3\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dd9\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2024 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0db1\u0dd2 04"
